acceptance_criteria:
Opening the web app shows the dashboard layout; an API call from the browser reaches the daemon only through the
web app's origin; a streamed SSE response passes through the proxy without buffering (test with a sample endpoint);
the daemon address is configurable.

With "notify when a bot finishes" on, a completed bot turn delivers one Slack message with a link to the thread;
an incident opening delivers to the configured channel; with no Slack identity the rule shows a delivery failure;
tests cover matching and single delivery.

Two monitors with different intervals fire at their own cadence; editing an interval changes the cadence without
a restart; a slow check does not overlap with the next; after a restart each monitor has exactly one schedule;
history is pruned; tests use fake timers.

Starting a bot session creates a worktree on a new branch and a session whose working directory is that
worktree; `bd create` by the agent lands in the main checkout list; the main checkout's git status is untouched;
a persona-missing bot fails to start with that reason; closing releases the lease.

Creating a bot with a missing Slack key returns status warnings naming the key; choosing a family whose plugin
is unhealthy is rejected; blank base branch resolves to the repository default; secrets never appear in responses;
tests cover status computation.

Acquiring a lease creates a worktree on a fresh branch from the base; resuming by holder returns the same path;
a second acquire beyond the cap is refused; the main checkout's branch and status are unchanged after acquire and
release; tests run against a temporary git repo.

Integration test (skipped when the CLIs are absent) runs a prompt through each family and receives text events;
loading a session by upstream id continues the conversation; cancel stops a running turn; the child environment
contains no variable from a denylist; stopping the daemon leaves no orphan processes.

Creating an instance with a secret stores it encrypted and every subsequent response shows only "set"; test
connection records healthy or the failure reason; deleting removes the secrets; a disallowed scope is rejected;
tests cover each.
